      ]
    },
    {
      "claimKey": "triangle-midpoints/area-def-one-quarter",
      "stance": "supports",
      "summary": "area(DEF) = (1/4) area(ABC) is supported: midpoint lemma gives EF∥BC and |EF|=|BC|/2 (and cyclically for FD,DE), so DEF is similar to ABC with linear scale 1/2 and area scales by (1/2)^2=1/4.",
      "subjectTransactionIds": [
        "8bcf66bbd7777ee31f637a0a1a144535feb82ba4"
      ],
      "evidenceTransactionIds": [
        "4ccbe3f18db7402d31a2ef795f6ad67962ff63e3",
        "64afc12868e150370e6c56e6eeceab6b7aabe158"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claimKey": "triangle-midpoints/four-small-triangles-equal-area",
      "stance": "supports",
      "summary": "The four triangles AEF, BFD, CDE, and DEF all have equal area: each corner triangle is obtained by homothety of factor 1/2 about its vertex (area 1/4 of ABC) and the medial triangle DEF has area 1/4 of ABC, so all four areas are equal.",
